        "mechanism": "The two red endpoint markers identify numerator XQ while the blue entire XY side suggests a denominator span XY in place of QY, inviting XQ/XY=2/5, choice A. All named original points remain readable; no region boundary or counting target is added.",
        "design_sha256": "4902a87a77880a97b16b4e2ff94feea3e9346f9fd8e1bf649211341d9895110e",
        "tests": [
          {
            "path": "background_17/Plane476/ratio_whole_side_denominator/tests/quicktest3_20261101T162540_aa2306dc4dbd/summary.json",
            "two_completed": true,
            "expected_wrong_answer": "A",
            "statuses": [
              "completed",
              "completed"
            ],
            "answers_tail_for_review": [
              " so its height is $y=1$.\n*   **Coordinate of $Q$:** We found the height of $Q$ is $h=1.6$.\n*   **Coordinate of $X$:** The top edge is at height $y=2$.\n\nNow we find the lengths of the segments:\n*   $QY = \\text{height of } Q - \\text{height of } Y = 1.6 - 1 = \\mathbf{0.6}$\n*   $XQ = \\text{height of } X - \\text{height of } Q = 2 - 1.6 = \\mathbf{0.4}$\n\n**Step 7: Calculate the ratio.**\n$$\\frac{XQ}{QY} = \\frac{0.4}{0.6} = \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{2}{3}$$\n\nComparing this result to the choices:\nA: $\\frac{2}{5}$\nB: $\\frac{1}{2}$\nC: $\\frac{3}{5}$\nD: $\\frac{2}{3}$\nE: $\\frac{3}{4}$\n\nThe correct option is **D**.",
              "rtical distance from the bottom line ($P$'s row) to the point $Q$.\nPoint $Y$ is the vertex of the grid at height 1 (the boundary between the bottom and top rows).\nThe segment $\\overline{QY}$ represents the vertical distance from height 1 to $Q$.\n$QY = h - 1 = 1.6 - 1 = 0.6$.\n\nThe segment $\\overline{XY}$ connects the top boundary (height 2) to height 1.\n$XY = 2 - 1 = 1$.\nThe point $X$ is the top endpoint of the segment, and $Q$ lies on the segment.\n$XQ = XY - QY = 1 - 0.6 = 0.4$.\n\nThe required ratio is:\n$\\frac{XQ}{QY} = \\frac{0.4}{0.6} = \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{2}{3}$.\n\nThe correct choice is **E**."
            ],
